Short:        VLC media player, unofficial OS3 port
Uploader:     (Dale fills this in at upload time)
Author:       VideoLAN (VLC); Amiga port: Dale Kirkwood
Type:         gfx/show
Version:      0.1
Requires:     OpenRTG, OpenGPU, OpenMedia, AHI; OpenSocket for streams
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Distribution: Aminet

An unofficial port of the VLC media player to AmigaOS 3.x, not made or
endorsed by VideoLAN.

A GadTools interface, with the drawing left to OpenRTG and OpenGPU: frames
stay in video RAM and are converted, scaled and composited by the graphics
board, subtitles and the on-screen display are alpha surfaces over the
picture, and full screen opens on any monitor. Decoding goes through OpenMedia
(the graphics chip's video engines, the PC's on AmigaChrome, a PiStorm's
VideoCore, or FFmpeg on the CPU), sound through AHI and network streams
through OpenSocket. Picasso96 and CyberGraphX systems get a slower fallback.

Status: planned; this readme is ready for the first release.

Licences: our Amiga modules are MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Dalsin Limited. VLC's
own code keeps its licences: libVLC, libvlccore and most modules are LGPL 2.1
